Implement and test Heaven Local Bridge v3 in repository fengie/mhw-mods, branch heaven-bridge only. Do real code work; do not just report recommendations.

Context:
- GitHub is repository truth.
- Live v2 worker currently runs from C:\Users\Xxkan\.mhw-local-tools\heaven-desktop-worker.py and supports protocol chatgpt-heaven-bridge-v2.
- The branch's heaven-bridge/worker.py is stale v1. Replace it with a hardened v3 based on the live v2 implementation.
- Do NOT modify main/master or any canonical branch.
- Do NOT restart/kill/replace the currently running bridge worker during this job. Only prepare code/config/tests in the heaven-bridge branch and push the commit(s).
- Keep secrets out of code, queue, results, logs, and commits.

Implement a meaningful production hardening set, preserving existing v2 protocol compatibility:
1) health capability/version negotiation (worker_version 3, protocol remains chatgpt-heaven-bridge-v2);
2) structured error objects/codes;
3) job TTL/future-skew validation and replay/duplicate/idempotency protection using canonical job hashes;
4) optional HMAC-SHA256 job verification when HEAVEN_BRIDGE_HMAC_KEY is configured, without breaking unsigned compatibility when it is not configured; health must report auth mode;
5) concurrent job execution with a bounded worker pool while serializing Git operations safely;
6) robust git retry/backoff/conflict handling and atomic local result writes before publish;
7) fs_delete and fs_copy with safe recursive semantics and dangerous-root protections;
8) fs_read_binary and fs_write_binary using chunked base64, plus improved text/file pagination;
9) output persistence/pagination for synchronous commands (return output metadata and expose a job_output_read action);
10) proc_kill must terminate the process tree on Windows; add per-session idle/maximum timeout cleanup and richer session telemetry;
11) environment handling that can inherit named local env vars by name without returning their values; reject obviously secret env values supplied inline;
12) cancellation action for running jobs where practical, plus job_status/progress metadata;
13) periodic worker heartbeat/capabilities publication under heaven-bridge/status with a conservative interval to avoid commit spam;
14) local sanitized JSONL audit log and rate limiting;
15) configurable allowed filesystem roots for structured fs_* actions, with safe defaults that include the user home, repo checkout, and C:\HeavenServices when present;
16) limit raw shell fallback in documentation and metadata: structured actions first; keep legacy raw actions for compatibility/recovery;
17) safe screenshot action if reliable in the interactive user session: save a PNG locally and return path/metadata so fs_read_binary can retrieve it. Do not implement clipboard reading by default.
18) update heaven-bridge/bootstrap.ps1 so a clean login/reboot installs/updates worker.py to the local runtime path, syntax-checks it, and configures reliable user-level startup/recovery. Preserve current GitHub relay fallback.
19) update heaven-bridge/README.md with architecture, protocol, security model, new actions, startup/recovery, and explicit no-public-raw-shell rule.
20) add automated tests covering TTL, duplicate hashing, path protections, binary roundtrip helpers, delete/copy safety, error-code structure, and capability health where testable without GitHub/network.

Run tests and python syntax checks locally on heaven. Commit and push changes to branch heaven-bridge. Return concise summary, changed files, test commands/results, and commit SHA.
